    },
    "message": "Store the index's key-only tables without rowids, and read a row's strings with less work\n\nentities and tokens are only their primary keys, so each row went into two B-trees. An\nindex file made before keeps its tables and answers the same.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
